import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 662 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 663 | 2026-10-26 | **Chapter 5's Workbook and teacher's copy (the decision board's build queue, item 2; tasks 171-172).** Built on row 662. Seven Workbook pages, each facing its Lesson Book page, fixed items so the teacher's copy always matches (HP_WB): p.2 C position (which finger plays the coral key, six cells; a week's log; colour C position on a blank keyboard and number the fingers), p.3 G position (which finger, six; where is C in G position: right 4, left 2; the letter ladder G _ B _ D), p.4 Move between them (which position and which hand from five coloured keys; lift, travel, land log; trace the bridge from C to G), p.5 Hands together (mirror twins: the other hand's same finger, which letter; log; draw both hands thumbs touching), p.6 Taking turns (call and answer: the left hand's finger numbers for the right hand's letters; make your own echo), p.7 Tunes (missing finger numbers in the chapter's tunes; a week's log; write your own tune, ending on 1), p.8 the check-up on paper (A C position fingers, B G position fingers, C position and hand, D mirror twins, E missing numbers in step-only rows, four each, 20 marks). Teacher's copy: answers, what to watch for and what to say for every page; marking and where to go back. Also fixed: Chapter 5's contents list in Korean (row 662). Files: drills.html, drills.src.html, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/patch687.py, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/hpw.jsx. |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
